      "reasons": [
        "The packet text provided only states that the study was a “meta-analysis” that “systematically evaluate[s] the effects of exercise interventions” and explores “dose–response relationships,” but it does not explicitly support the definition’s broader claim that a meta-analysis is a general “research method … across studies.”",
        "The definition’s wording that it evaluates “an intervention or other factor” is broader than what the packet supports (the packet specifically references exercise interventions and sleep quality in patients with depression).",
